  <!-- 2. Estimated vs reconstructed -->
  <section class="lp-section hw-compare">
    <div class="lp-shell">
      <p class="lp-eyebrow">A different starting point</p>
      <h2 class="lp-h2">The maps look alike. The foundations don't.</h2>
      <div class="hw-questions">
        <div><span>Other tools ask</span><strong>What does the process usually look like?</strong></div>
        <div><span>RE-ViVE answers</span><strong>What happened to this loan, this payment, this customer, and why?</strong></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hw-columns">
        <div class="hw-col">
          <h3>Discovery-first (statistical)</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>Start from an event log and one chosen case perspective</li>
            <li>Discover, abstract and simplify a process model</li>
            <li>Explain the paths and exceptions around that model</li>
          </ol>
          <p>Aggregation and filtering can hide low-frequency behavior and the links between objects, which is exactly where banking risk sits.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hw-col hw-col-us">
          <h3>Execution-first (RE-ViVE)</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>Start from operational events, identities and relationships</li>
            <li>Deterministically reconstruct each execution</li>
            <li>Show paths, exceptions and context you can verify</li>
          </ol>
          <p>No predefined ideal process and no statistically representative path. The map is the result, not the assumption.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Why it is hard to copy -->
  <section class="lp-section hw-hard">
    <div class="lp-shell">
      <p class="lp-eyebrow">Why this is hard to copy</p>
      <h2 class="lp-h2">Four problems the category still struggles with. Solved on one foundation.</h2>
      <div class="hw-grid4">
        <div class="hw-item">
          <p class="hw-num">01 · Concurrency</p>
          <h3>Parallel work is not rework.</h3>
          <p>Sanctions screening and ID verification can finish in either order. Other approaches can draw that as a loop. RE-ViVE recognizes them as peers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hw-item">
          <p class="hw-num">02 · Context</p>
          <h3>Any business view, same evidence.</h3>
          <p>Product, channel, branch, risk tier, relationship manager, policy version. Dozens of dimensions without rebuilding the execution for each view.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hw-item">
          <p class="hw-num">03 · Change</p>
          <h3>When the workflow changes, the view does too.</h3>
          <p>A new fraud check added in Q2 shows up in Q2, not as noise across the year. New and retired steps compare cleanly over time.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hw-item">
          <p class="hw-num">04 · AI agents</p>
          <h3>Agents tied to business outcomes.</h3>
          <p>Agent runs, tool calls and retries link to the loans, cases and payments they touched, so an extraction agent's retries trace to the disputes that missed their deadline.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hw-minis">
        <figure><svg aria-label="One start splits into parallel KYC and credit checks before joining for approval" role="img" viewbox="0 0 270 125"><g fill="none" stroke="#368c87" stroke-width="3"><path d="M24 63 H65 L91 31 H172 L198 63 H244"></path><path d="M65 63 L91 96 H172 L198 63"></path></g><g fill="#fff" stroke="#167f79" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="24" cy="63" r="8"></circle><circle cx="244" cy="63" r="8"></circle><rect height="28" rx="7" width="83" x="90" y="17"></rect><rect height="28" rx="7" width="83" x="90" y="82"></rect></g><g fill="#23465d" font-size="10" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><text x="131" y="35">KYC</text><text x="131" y="100">Credit</text><text x="24" y="82">Start</text><text x="244" y="82">Approve</text></g></svg><figcaption>Independent checks, not a false rework loop</figcaption></figure>
        <figure><svg aria-label="One common execution line viewed through three business dimensions" role="img" viewbox="0 0 270 125"><path d="M20 60 H250" stroke="#b3c8d8" stroke-width="4"></path><g fill="#167f79"><circle cx="38" cy="60" r="9"></circle><circle cx="105" cy="60" r="9"></circle><circle cx="172" cy="60" r="9"></circle><circle cx="239" cy="60" r="9"></circle></g><g font-size="11" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><rect fill="#e6f3ef" height="26" rx="13" width="77" x="8" y="6"></rect><text fill="#167f79" x="46" y="23">Product</text><rect fill="#e9effa" height="26" rx="13" width="77" x="96" y="6"></rect><text fill="#3276b4" x="134" y="23">Channel</text><rect fill="#efe9f9" height="26" rx="13" width="77" x="184" y="6"></rect><text fill="#7653a7" x="222" y="23">Risk tier</text></g><path d="M46 32 V48 M134 32 V48 M222 32 V48" stroke="#9eb8c9" stroke-dasharray="3 3"></path></svg><figcaption>Different business views of the same executions</figcaption></figure>
        <figure><svg aria-label="Earlier period has three activities and later period adds a fraud review" role="img" viewbox="0 0 270 125"><g fill="none" stroke="#b3c8d8" stroke-width="3"><path d="M25 37 H245"></path><path d="M25 91 H245"></path></g><g fill="#167f79"><circle cx="35" cy="37" r="8"></circle><circle cx="135" cy="37" r="8"></circle><circle cx="235" cy="37" r="8"></circle><circle cx="35" cy="91" r="8"></circle><circle cx="105" cy="91" r="8"></circle><circle cx="235" cy="91" r="8"></circle></g><circle cx="172" cy="91" fill="#db9c45" r="9"></circle><g fill="#284963" font-size="10" font-weight="700"><text x="10" y="17">Q1</text><text x="10" y="72">Q2</text><text x="149" y="114">New fraud check</text></g></svg><figcaption>New steps appear when the process changes</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. Evidence -->
  <section class="lp-section hw-evidence">
    <div class="lp-shell hw-split">
      <div>
        <p class="lp-eyebrow">Built for scrutiny</p>
        <h2 class="lp-h2">Every path counted. When the examiner asks, open the record.</h2>
        <p class="lp-lead">Rare paths are where the risk, the cost and the complaints live. RE-ViVE keeps the whole in-scope population, reconciles it against the source, and lets a team go from a pattern to a single request in loan origination, core banking, payments or case management.</p>
        <div class="hw-recon" aria-label="Illustrative population reconciliation: 100,000 in scope, 100,000 accounted for">
          <div class="hw-recon-head"><span>In scope <strong>100,000</strong></span><span>Accounted for <strong>100,000</strong></span></div>
          <div class="hw-recon-bar"><i style="width:72%"></i><i style="width:17%"></i><i style="width:8%"></i><i style="width:3%"></i></div>
          <div class="hw-recon-keys"><span>72% standard</span><span>17% rework</span><span>8% exception</span><span>3% other</span></div>
          <p class="hw-cap">Illustration · population reconciliation</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="hw-figure">
